# motion (Cursor rules export)

The condensed form of the `motion` skill — the full skill lives at github.com/lucasgabrieldevgg/motion; this file carries the operating rules.

## The motion contract

1. Every animation answers a purpose: feedback, continuity, orientation, hierarchy, or rationed delight. Otherwise cut.
2. Composite-only per frame: `transform` + `opacity`. Layout properties never animate; shadows/blurs animate as cross-faded pseudo-element opacity.
3. Duration bands: micro 100–250ms · UI 200–300ms · page 300–500ms · nothing user-waits-on > 500ms · scroll/ambient is progress-based.
4. Enter eases out, exit eases in, exit is shorter and subtler. Scroll-scrub is `linear`; `linear` on UI state is a defect.
5. `prefers-reduced-motion` is tiered, never a kill switch: Tier 1 (parallax, large slides, 3D, marquees, smooth-scroll, custom cursor) removed; Tier 2 (small movement) → ≤200ms fade; Tier 3 (opacity, color, focus rings, spinners) kept. JS-driven motion gated via `matchMedia` — CSS alone never covers timelines/canvas.
6. Never ship unverified: freeze-frame screenshots of start/mid/end, both motion paths.

## The craft core

- Frequency law: 1000×/day → 100ms opacity; 1×/ever → 600ms choreography.
- Easing library: snappy `(0.2,0,0,1)` · enter `(0.16,1,0.3,1)` · exit `(0.55,0,1,0.45)` · overshoot `(0.34,1.56,0.64,1)` · move `(0.4,0,0.2,1)`.
- Springs (Motion): snappy 400/30 · tactile 500/30 · bouncy 300/12–18 · drag-follow 800+/35–40. Springs ignore duration.
- Stagger: 30–80ms/item, 2–4 items mid-flight, total ≤ 400ms in waiting contexts. CSS: `calc(sibling-index() * 60ms)`.
- One director: one primary motion at a time; page declares a motion budget.
- State continuity: loading→success is one object morphing, not jump cuts.
- Slop death list: perpetual loops · same fade-up everywhere · `scale(0)` · linear UI easing · bounce-everything · parallax on text · >1 marquee · glow/blob motion · unpauseable autoplay · `transition: all` · scroll-hijack without escape · hover that moves the click target · animation after content is readable.

## Technology choice

State pair → CSS `transition`. Appear/disappear → `@starting-style` + `allow-discrete`. Scroll-driven → `animation-timeline` in `@supports` (content visible by default). Page/route → View Transitions API. Sequence/pin/cinematic scrub → GSAP + ScrollTrigger (`ease: "none"` on containers, `quickTo` for followers, `useGSAP` in React). React state/exit/shared-layout/drag → Motion (`AnimatePresence` + stable `key`; `stagger()` not deprecated `staggerChildren`; `MotionConfig reducedMotion="user"`). Layout change → FLIP or Motion `layout`. Icon draw/morph → SVG (`pathLength="1"` trick; MorphSVG/flubber for mismatched). Particles → Canvas (DPR-aware, loop pauses offscreen, never starts under reduce). 3D/shaders → three/R3F (dispose, DPR ≤ 2, gate loop). AE animation → Lottie dotLottie (`setFrame` for scroll). Interactive state machines → Rive.

## Integration rules

- Values are tokens: `--dur-*`, `--ease-*`, one stagger value. Two durations + three easings cover 90%.
- Batch DOM reads, then writes — interleaved reads/writes are layout thrashing.
- `will-change` just-in-time, removed when idle.
- Animations never change layout (CLS 0): containers reserve final space.
- Keyboard/screen-reader parity: state never lives only in the animation; focus indicators survive every frame.
- Smooth-scroll libs never instantiate under reduce. Autoplay > 5s needs a visible pause.
- Verify: `?t=`/`?state=`/`?reduce=1` freeze harness + Playwright screenshots both paths; DevTools Performance shows no per-frame Layout/Paint.

## Final gate

> Could a reviewer freeze any frame, see intent — and does the reduced-motion path still communicate everything without teleporting anyone?

If not, it's not done. Motion ships at *physical and verified* — not at *plausible*.

